The attached image (Fig. 6) illustrates that Nano-11 improves antigen targeting to immunopotentiating cells in the draining lymph node and enhances antigen retention at the injection site. Panel A shows that OVA-positive migratory dendritic cells (MigDCs) exhibit the highest expression of the costimulatory molecule CD86 compared to lymphoid tissue resident DCs and monocytes/macrophages. Panel B further characterizes OVA-positive MigDCs as predominantly CD11b+. Panel C, through in vivo imaging, demonstrates that Nano-11 significantly prolongs the presence of Alexa Fluor 647-conjugated OVA at the injection site over 7 days, compared to soluble OVA or OVA combined with aluminum hydroxide. These results underscore Nano-11's efficacy in antigen delivery and retention, critical for robust immune activation.